{{!-- The three debilities, as bands under the stats row. Params: debilities.

      Each band spans the two stats it hinders: the pairs the rules use are contiguous in the row
      (str+dex, int+wis, con+cha) and cover all six exactly once, so three equal thirds of the stats
      block land one band under each pair without anything having to measure a tile.

      Two groups, not four siblings: the divider art and the tick it frames belong to one band, and
      the name sits below it in normal flow. Everything used to be absolutely positioned against
      hand-measured pixel offsets, so the name climbed into the art as soon as Foundry's font
      setting grew it. --}}
<div class="stonetop-debilities">
	{{#each debilities}}
	<div class="stonetop-debility{{#if active}} is-active{{/if}}">
		<label class="stonetop-debility-control"
		       data-tooltip="{{description}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP">
			<span class="stonetop-debility-band">
				<span class="stonetop-debility-divider"></span>
				<input type="checkbox" class="stonetop-debility-check"
				       data-change-action="debility"
				       data-slug="{{key}}"
				       aria-describedby="{{@root.sheetIdPrefix}}-debility-{{key}}"
				       {{#if active}}checked{{/if}}>
			</span>
			<span class="stonetop-debility-label">{{name}}</span>
			{{!-- What it DOES, in the DOM in both states and drawn in neither.

			      Ticked, it used to be a sentence of rules text under the name — and three of them
			      took the band from 34px to 98px, shoving the picture, the tabs and the whole sheet
			      down at the moment a fight is going badly. The band is a row of bracket art under a
			      row of tiles; it cannot also be a rules reference.

			      Not deleted, though: the hover is pointer-bound and invisible to assistive tech, so
			      the sentence stays here, clipped, and the tick is described BY it. That is the same
			      device the folded line uses to name the debility that dimmed a stat — a colour, or a
			      hover, is never the only carrier of anything. --}}
			<span class="stonetop-debility-effect" id="{{@root.sheetIdPrefix}}-debility-{{key}}">{{description}}</span>
		</label>
	</div>
	{{/each}}
</div>
